.TH BYTE_LOWER 3
.SH NAME
byte_lower \- convert a byte array to lowercase
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <byte.h>
.PP
.BI "void byte_lower(void* " s ", size_t " len ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B byte_lower
converts all uppercase ASCII characters ('A'-'Z') within the memory area
pointed to by
.I s
of length
.I len
to their corresponding lowercase ASCII characters ('a'-'z').
.PP
The conversion is performed in-place. Other characters remain unchanged. The function does not assume any locale-specific behavior and is restricted to the standard ASCII character set.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR byte_upper (3)